# =====================================================================
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT (allowlist) ignore rules.
#
# Everything is ignored unless explicitly re-included with a `!` rule.
# Tracking a new file therefore requires a visible, deliberate change to
# this file - a secret dropped into the tree can never be committed
# silently (it simply won't show up in `git status`).
# =====================================================================

# ignore everything by default
*

# ...but always re-include directories, so files inside them can be
# allowed one by one
!**/

# repository control files
!.gitignore
!Makefile
!README.md
!flake.nix
!flake.lock
!**/*.md
!**/*.toml

# Nix sources
!**/*.nix

# age-encrypted secrets (ciphertext only - safe to version)
!**/*.age

# public key material and signed certificates (public - safe to version)
!**/*.pub
!**/*-cert.pub

# anything else (private keys, .pem, tokens, dotenv, archives, ...)
# stays ignored until you deliberately whitelist it above.